%% M8 sequence: register an endpoint and send a test ping. Planned design: follows contracts/openapi/webhook-service.v1.yaml and issue #21.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P0 as Merchant
    participant P1 as Merchant page<br/>+ BFF
    participant P2 as api-gateway
    participant P3 as webhook-service
    participant P4 as MongoDB<br/>webhooks
    participant P5 as Redis<br/>BullMQ
        P0->>P1: enter https URL and event types
        P1->>P2: POST /api/v1/webhooks/endpoints (bearer, via BFF)
        P2->>P3: forward (JWT valid)
        P3->>P3: role MERCHANT, merchant_id comes from the token, never the body
        P3->>P3: validate URL: https in production, resolve host, block private, loopback and link-local IPs
        alt URL rejected or body invalid
            P3-->>P1: 400 problem+json
        else URL accepted
            P3->>P3: generate random secret, encrypt it for storage
            P3->>P4: insert endpoint (secret_enc, event_types, active)
            P4-->>P3: endpointId
            P3-->>P1: 201 endpoint + secret (returned only this once)
            P1-->>P0: show the secret once, with a copy button
        end
        P0->>P1: click Send test ping
        P1->>P3: POST /endpoints/{id}/test via gateway
        P3->>P4: find endpoint by id AND merchant_id
        P4-->>P3: endpoint, or nothing
        alt other merchant's endpoint or unknown id
            P3-->>P1: 404 problem+json (existence is not revealed)
        else own endpoint
            P3->>P4: insert delivery (status PENDING)
            P3->>P5: enqueue delivery job
            P3-->>P1: 202 Queued, the worker sends the signed ping
        end
